;;;; Russian translations. Each entry is (ENGLISH TRANSLATION); the English text is the key.
;;;; A translation asks for the same format directives, in the same order, as its English text.
;;;; Russian has three forms of a noun after a number (1, 2-4, 5 and more); a format directive can only tell
;;;; 0, 1 and the others, so where the English text says "~d entities" or "~d entity" the translation names
;;;; what it counts before the number ("Objects: 3"), which is right for every number, and keeps the
;;;; directives of the plural so that the translation asks for the same values.
;;;; The file is UTF-8 data: it is read, never evaluated.

(:language :ru-ru
 :name "Русский (Россия)"
 :entries
